'''Kim Hyo-jung''' ({{korean|김효정}}; born December 11, 1990), better known by her stage name '''Hyolyn''' ({{Korean|hangul=효린|labels=no}}), is a South Korean singer and songwriter. Currently, she is under the management of Bridʒ, a production company she founded herself.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://people.search.naver.com/search.naver?where=nexearch&query=%ED%9A%A8%EB%A6%B0&sm=tab_etc&ie=utf8&key=PeopleService&os=181579|script-title=ko:효린 :: 네이버 인물검색|website=people.search.naver.com|language=ko|access-date=2018-02-09|archive-date=November 11, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201111105716/https://people.search.naver.com/search.naver?where=nexearch&query=%ED%9A%A8%EB%A6%B0&sm=tab_etc&ie=utf8&key=PeopleService&os=181579|location=South Korea|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=468&aid=0000320400|script-title=ko:효린, 새로운 소속사 설립...본격적인 솔로활동 예고|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|location=South Korea|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122244/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=468&aid=0000320400|url-status=live}}</ref> She is a former member of the South Korean girl group [[Sistar]] and their sub-unit [[Sistar19]].

==Life and career==
===1990–2009: Early life and career beginnings===
Kim Hyo-jung was born on December 11, 1990, in [[Incheon]], South Korea. Her father is a retired [[Republic of Korea Marine Corps|Marine Corps]] officer.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.naver.com/main/read.nhn?mode=LSD&mid=sec&sid1=103&oid=375&aid=0000079647|script-title=ko:효린 통금시간 고백 "8시까지 통금, 아버지 무서워 대체로 지켜"|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=July 27, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210727075510/https://news.naver.com/main/read.nhn?mode=LSD&mid=sec&sid1=103&oid=375&aid=0000079647|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2013/06/25/2013062501510.html|script-title=ko:효린 고백,"화끈하게 놀고 화끈하게 혼나고"...'통금시간이 몇시였기에?'|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002257/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2013/06/25/2013062501510.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Born prematurely, Hyolyn's infancy was complicated by a serious form of [[biliary atresia]], which led to several surgeries, [[Intussusception (medical disorder)|intussuseption]] and the eventual loss of her gall bladder. She explained on the TV program ''[[Strong Heart (TV series)|Strong Heart]]'' in 2011 that she grew up a sickly child but has since regained most of her health.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://health.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2011/03/16/2011031602086.html|script-title=ko:'육상돌' 효린이 걸린 담도폐쇄증은? – 당신의 건강가이드 헬스조선|last=chosun|first=health|website=health.chosun.com|access-date=2018-02-09|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002240/http://health.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2011/03/16/2011031602086.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=015&aid=0002411485|script-title=ko:씨스타 효린 "담도폐쇄증에 장중첩증까지 앓았다" 충격 고백|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122233/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=015&aid=0002411485|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.naver.com/main/read.nhn?mode=LSD&mid=sec&sid1=102&oid=088&aid=0000189479|script-title=ko:효린 담도폐쇄증 사연 공개 ... "수술 후 목욕탕 갈 때 많은 상처"|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=018&aid=0002404442|script-title=ko:효린, 담도폐쇄증으로 `10시간 수술` 과거 털어놔|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122232/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=018&aid=0002404442|url-status=live}}</ref> Hyolyn has one younger sister, Kim Hye-jung.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=420&aid=0000000023|script-title=ko:[씨스타] 1부. 효린 VS 김효정|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122208/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=420&aid=0000000023|url-status=live}}</ref>

Hyolyn stated that she has loved singing and dancing since childhood and that no one was around to help her so she began picking up auditions on her own.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=009&aid=0002679283|script-title=ko:효린, 알고보니 'JYP오디션' 1등 합격자 출신|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122214/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=009&aid=0002679283|url-status=live}}</ref> She auditioned for [[JYP Entertainment]] two times before being accepted after placing first in the audition. She was set to debut in a project group with [[Secret (Korean band)|Secret]]'s [[Song Jieun|Jieun]], [[EXID]]'s [[Hani (singer)|Hani]], and [[Bestie (band)|Bestie]]'s Uji. However, plans for their debut were cancelled.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://en.asiatoday.co.kr/view.php?key=20150124001538588|title=SISTAR's Hyorin almost formed group with EXID's Hani and SECRET's Song Ji-eun|work=SISTAR's Hyorin revealed that she almost had formed a group with EXID's Hani and SECRET's Song Ji-eun.On the December 31st episode of Mnet's 'Beatles..|access-date=2018-02-08|language=en|archive-date=July 15, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150715102305/http://en.asiatoday.co.kr/view.php?key=20150124001538588|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=311&aid=0000434135|title=[Weekly★] EXID 하니, 이렇게 매력쟁이였나?|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122227/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=311&aid=0000434135|url-status=live}}</ref> Hyolyn then left JYP and joined [[Starship Entertainment]], auditioning with a cover of [[Christina Aguilera]]'s "[[Hurt (Christina Aguilera song)|Hurt]]".<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2010/04/21/2010042100515.html|script-title=ko:초특급 신인그룹 씨스타의 리더 효린, 폭발적 가창력 동영상 공개돼|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002253/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2010/04/21/2010042100515.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=001&aid=0003249010|script-title=ko:보라ㆍ효린 등 씨스타 멤버 네티즌 화제|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122211/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=001&aid=0003249010|url-status=live}}</ref> Starship began forming a new girl group in 2010, with Hyolyn as the leader. The group were praised for their fresh faces and vocal abilities.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2010/05/07/2010050700480.html|script-title=ko:씨스타 효린, '장근석의 그녀'로 관심몰이|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002241/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2010/05/07/2010050700480.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2010/06/09/2010060900842.html|script-title=ko:씨스타, 데뷔 후 주가 ↑ 'CF 러브콜 쇄도'|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002154/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2010/06/09/2010060900842.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Musicians face bullying accusations |url=http://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/article/Article.aspx?aid=3063523 |author=Lee Jae-lim |website=[[Korea JoongAng Daily]] |access-date=May 27, 2019 |language=en |date=May 27, 2019 |archive-date=May 26, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190526124906/http://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/news/article/article.aspx?aid=3063523 |url-status=live }}</ref>

===2010–2011: Debut with Sistar and Sistar19===
{{Main|Sistar}}
On June 3, 2010, Hyolyn made her debut as a member of Sistar on [[Korean Broadcasting System|KBS]]' ''[[Music Bank (TV program)|Music Bank]]'' with their debut single, "[[Push Push (Sistar song)|Push Push]]".<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=003&aid=0003273625|script-title=ko:씨스타, 데뷔합니다 'Push Push'|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122219/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=003&aid=0003273625|url-status=live}}</ref>

In early 2011, Hyolyn and group member [[Yoon Bo-ra|Bora]] formed the sub-group [[Sistar19]]. They released the successful single "[[Ma Boy]]" in 2011 and on October 17, 2011, Hyolyn released the single "Ma Boy 2", featuring Electroboyz.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=015&aid=0002591924|script-title=ko:'뮤직뱅크' 일렉트로보이즈, 효린의 빈자리는 없다 '한솥밥 식구들의 찰떡 호흡'|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122239/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=015&aid=0002591924|url-status=live}}</ref> Their first EP ''[[Gone Not Around Any Longer]]'', with a title track of the same name, was released in January 2013 and was met with success on several music charts.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2013/12/15/2013121500189.html|script-title=ko:씨스타19 '있다 없으니까', 美빌보드 K팝차트 2013년 '1위'|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002212/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2013/12/15/2013121500189.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2011/04/28/2011042800707.html|script-title=ko:씨스타, 새로운 유닛 '씨스타19' 결성|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002247/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2011/04/28/2011042800707.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

===2012–2014: First acting role and solo debut with ''Love & Hate''===
In 2012, Hyolyn starred in the KBS drama ''[[Dream High Season 2]]'' as Nana, a famous idol from the fictional girl group Hershe.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=015&aid=0002619818|script-title=ko:[포토] '드림하이2' 씨스타 효린, '손으로 살짝 가리고'|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122230/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=015&aid=0002619818|url-status=live}}</ref> She teamed up with [[Ailee]] and [[T-ara]]'s [[Park Ji-yeon|Jiyeon]] for the song "Superstar" for the soundtrack.<ref>{{in lang|ko}} [http://news.naver.com/main/read.nhn?mode=LSD&mid=sec&sid1=106&oid=108&aid=0002121587 효린 "'드림하이2' 출연, 노래보다 연기연습 많아"] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131016052306/http://news.naver.com/main/read.nhn?mode=LSD&mid=sec&sid1=106&oid=108&aid=0002121587 |date=October 16, 2013 }}. News.naver.com (January 17, 2012). Retrieved on 2012-07-17.</ref>

In August 2013, Hyolyn sang an OST for the [[Seoul Broadcasting System|SBS']] drama, ''[[Master's Sun]]'', titled "You Make Me Go Crazy".<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2013/08/21/2013082100523.html|script-title=ko:씨스타 뭐하나 했더니...효린, '주군의 태양' OST 발표|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002307/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2013/08/21/2013082100523.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2013/09/17/2013091703251.html|script-title=ko:'겁도 없이'... 서인국이 부른 '주군의태양' OST, 차트 1위!|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002313/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2013/09/17/2013091703251.html|url-status=live}}</ref> On November 22, she shared the stage with [[Stevie Wonder]] for a special performance of "[[I Just Called to Say I Love You]]" at the 2013 [[Mnet Asian Music Awards]], one of South Korea's biggest music award shows.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/stevie-wonder-k-pop-star-hyorin-to-duet-at-2013-mamas-5800462/|title=Stevie Wonder|magazine=Billboard|access-date=March 7, 2015|archive-date=September 24, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150924162842/http://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/k-town/5800462/stevie-wonder-k-pop-star-hyorin-to-duet-at-2013-mamas|url-status=live}}</ref> Hyolyn made her solo debut on November 26 with the album ''[[Love & Hate (Hyolyn album)|Love & Hate]]''.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://en.asiatoday.co.kr/view.php?key=900652|title=Hyolyn releases full version of "One Way Love" MV|work=SISTAR's Hyolyn released full version of her music video for her title track, One Way Love. On November 27, Hyolyn's agency Starship Entertai..|access-date=2018-02-09|language=en|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002313/http://en.asiatoday.co.kr/view.php?key=900652|url-status=live}}</ref> The album contained double title tracks, "Lonely" and "One Way Love", featuring Korean rappers [[Mad Clown]], [[Block B]]'s [[Zico (rapper)|Zico]], [[Dok2]], and [[Geeks (musical duo)|Geeks']] [[Lil Boi]], and some tracks produced by [[Brave Brothers]] and Kim Do-hoon.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=20131128000986&ACE_SEARCH=1|title=Eyelike: Hyolyn shows promise on "LOVE&HATE"|date=November 28, 2013|access-date=2018-02-08|language=en|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002230/http://www.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=20131128000986&ACE_SEARCH=1|url-status=live}}</ref> Both of the album's singles saw success, with "One Way Love" winning first place on several music shows, placing number one on [[Gaon Digital Chart|Gaon]]'s Weekly Digital Chart and number one on Billboard's [[Kpop Hot 100|K-Pop Hot 100]], with "Lonely" falling at number four and number three respectively.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=8245|title=Hyorin Won on Mnet M Countdown Chart of This Week|website=BNTNews UK|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209182338/http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=8245|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=8083|title=Hyorin Won on Show Champion with 'One Way Love'|website=BNTNews UK|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209182356/http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=8083|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://gaonchart.co.kr/main/section/chart/online.gaon?nationGbn=T&serviceGbn=ALL&targetTime=49&hitYear=2013&termGbn=week|script-title=ko:국내 대표 음악 차트 가온차트!|website=[[Gaon Chart]]|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=November 7, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201107113056/http://gaonchart.co.kr/main/section/chart/online.gaon?nationGbn=T&serviceGbn=ALL&targetTime=49&hitYear=2013&termGbn=week|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/k-pop-hot-100-hyorin-sends-her-one-way-love-to-no-1-2ne1-stays-5819684/|title=K-Pop Hot 100: Hyorin Sends Her 'One Way Love' to No. 1, 2NE1 Stays Strong at No. 2|magazine=Billboard|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=May 18, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180518083559/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/k-town/5819684/k-pop-hot-100-hyorin-sends-her-one-way-love-to-no-1-2ne1-stays|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=8116|title=SISTAR's Hyolyn Ranked on the 1st Place of Billboard K-POP Chart|website=BNTNews UK|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209182403/http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=8116|url-status=live}}</ref> On December 31, the music video for the Korean version of "[[Let It Go (Disney song)|Let It Go]]" for [[The Walt Disney Company|Disney]]'s animated film ''[[Frozen (2013 film)|Frozen]],'' sung by Hyolyn, was revealed.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=9756|title=Korean Version of 'Frozen' Soundtrack Album to Be Released|website=BNTNews UK|access-date=2018-02-09|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209182321/http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=9756|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2014/02/11/2014021101347.html|script-title=ko:효린 Let It go, 애절한 음색의 겨울왕국은? ... "이것이 진짜다"|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002251/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2014/02/11/2014021101347.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2014/01/22/2014012202505.html|script-title=ko:효린, 스크린-안방 OST 동시 석권..'겨울왕국' & '별그대'|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002228/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2014/01/22/2014012202505.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

[[File:Hyolyn at Hanyang University Festival in September 2014 04.jpg|thumb|Hyolyn performing in 2014|alt=|upright]]
In January 2014, Hyolyn released an OST for the drama ''[[My Love from the Star]]'' titled "Goodbye".<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2014/01/22/2014012201822.html|script-title=ko:씨스타 효린, '별그대' OST 참여 '안녕', 음원공개 '화제'|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002216/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2014/01/22/2014012201822.html|url-status=live}}</ref> On March 28, Starship Entertainment announced on their Twitter account that Hyolyn would feature in Mad Clown's comeback track, "Without You", released on April 3.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=16991|title=Mad Clown Is About To Come Back!|website=BNTNews UK|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209182324/http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=16991|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2014/04/04/2014040402228.html|script-title=ko:매드클라운, 씨스타 효린과 즐거운 녹음현장 공개|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002311/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2014/04/04/2014040402228.html|url-status=live}}</ref> She also participated in rapper [[MC Mong]]'s comeback to the Korean scene after five years with the album ''Miss Me or Diss Me,'' released on November 3.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.mwave.me/en/news/news/view/79287/MC-Mong-to-Return-with-Album-%E2%80%98Miss-Me-or-Diss-Me%E2%80%99-in-Early-November|title=MC Mong to Return with Album 'Miss Me or Diss Me' in Early November {{!}} Mwave|website=www.mwave.me|language=en|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209002802/https://www.mwave.me/en/news/news/view/79287/MC-Mong-to-Return-with-Album-%E2%80%98Miss-Me-or-Diss-Me%E2%80%99-in-Early-November|url-status=live}}</ref> On November 20, she collaborated with singer-songwriter and fellow label mate, [[Jooyoung]], on a track titled "Erase" ({{Korean|hangul=지워|labels=no}}) featuring Iron, which peaked at number nine on the Gaon Weekly chart.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2014/11/20/2014112002549.html|script-title=ko:효린-주영, 이건 '특급' 콜라보레이션이야|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002303/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2014/11/20/2014112002549.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://gaonchart.co.kr/main/section/chart/online.gaon?nationGbn=T&serviceGbn=ALL&targetTime=49&hitYear=2014&termGbn=week|script-title=ko:국내 대표 음악 차트 가온차트!|website=[[Gaon Chart]]|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=April 2, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160402145418/http://gaonchart.co.kr/main/section/chart/online.gaon?serviceGbn=ALL&termGbn=week&hitYear=2014&targetTime=49&nationGbn=T|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2014/11/26/2014112600680.html|script-title=ko:효린-주영, "우리 첫 방송에 1위 했어요" 자축|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002226/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2014/11/26/2014112600680.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Hyolyn was the first idol group singer to participate in the Chuseok special of the music variety show ''[[I Am a Singer]]'' that aired on September 9. She ranked second overall.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.naver.com/main/read.nhn?mode=LSD&mid=sec&sid1=103&oid=015&aid=0003153441|script-title=ko:'나는 가수다 추석특집' 효린, '귀로' 열창 이후 눈물 쏟아...왜?|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=July 27, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210727075519/https://news.naver.com/main/read.nhn?mode=LSD&mid=sec&sid1=103&oid=015&aid=0003153441|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=213&aid=0000543163|script-title=ko:'나는가수다' 효린, 1위보다 값진 2위...아이돌 넘어 뮤지션|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122227/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=213&aid=0000543163|url-status=live}}</ref>

===2015–2016: ''It's Me''===
[[File:씨스타(SISTAR) G페스티벌 아시아 드림 콘서트 (7) (cropped).jpg|thumb|upright|left|Hyolyn performing at the G Festival Asia Dream Concert in 2016]]
On January 13, it was revealed that Hyolyn was to join [[MBC TV (South Korean TV channel)|MBC]]'s ''I Am a Singer'' Season 3 as the first idol singer to feature on the show.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.mwave.me/kr/news/news/view/85003/SISTAR%E2%80%B2s-Hyolyn-Confirms-for-%E2%80%B2I-Am-a-Singer-3%E2%80%B2|title=SISTAR′s Hyolyn Confirms for ′I Am a Singer 3′ {{!}} Mwave|website=www.mwave.me|language=ko|access-date=2018-02-08}}{{Dead link|date=August 2024 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref> She was the first contestant eliminated from the show but still impressed viewers with her song choices, especially her emotional rendition of [[Lee Sun-hee (singer)|Lee Sun-hee]]'s classic ballad "Fate", which brought the audience to tears.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2015/02/13/2015021303757.html|script-title=ko:'나가수3' 효린, 완벽한 재해석..이보다 좋을 순 없다|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=July 7, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180707010041/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2015/02/13/2015021303757.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.naver.com/main/read.nhn?mode=LSD&mid=sec&sid1=004&oid=215&aid=0000267232|script-title=ko:'나는 가수다3', 아이돌 넘어 가수 효린의 무한한 가능성|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=July 27, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210727075510/https://news.naver.com/main/read.nhn?mode=LSD&mid=sec&sid1=004&oid=215&aid=0000267232|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2015/02/13/2015021303870.html|script-title=ko:'나가수3', 스윗소로우 1위 '이변'..효린 첫 탈락자 [종합]|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=July 6, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180706190618/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2015/02/13/2015021303870.html|url-status=live}}</ref> On April 2, Hyolyn teamed up with her bandmate [[Soyou]] to cover [[K.Will]]'s song "Growing" as Starship Entertainment's cover project.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.mwave.me/kr/news/news/view/90553/%5BVideo%5D-SISTAR%E2%80%B2s-Soyou-and-Hyolyn-Beautifully-Cover-K.Will%E2%80%B2s-%E2%80%B2Growing%E2%80%B2|title=[Video] SISTAR′s Soyou and Hyolyn Beautifully Cover K.Will′s ′Growing′ {{!}} Mwave|website=www.mwave.me|language=ko|access-date=2018-02-08}}{{Dead link|date=January 2023 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=19462|title=Hyolyn & SoYou Cover K.Will's 'Growing'|website=BNTNews UK|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209182329/http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=19462|url-status=live}}</ref> On August 17, it was revealed that Hyolyn was to join ''[[Unpretty Rapstar]]'' Season 2.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://english.yonhapnews.co.kr/search1/2603000000.html?cid=AEN20150908005051315|title=Yonhap News Agency|website=[[Yonhap News Agency]]|language=en|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122238/http://english.yonhapnews.co.kr/search1/2603000000.html?cid=AEN20150908005051315|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2015/09/22/2015092200628.html|script-title=ko:[애프터스토리]효린의 '언프리티랩스타2' 출연, 옳은 선택이었나?|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002249/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2015/09/22/2015092200628.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Hyolyn released her Unpretty Rapstar's semi-finals track "My Love" featuring [[Basick]] on November 6, 2015. She finished the show in third place. On December 14, Hyolyn, Jooyoung, and [[Bumkey]] collaborated with producing team [[Da Internz]] on the song "Love Line".<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=27247|title=Hyolyn, Jooyoung and Bumkey to Release 'LOVELINE'|website=BNTNews UK|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209182400/http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=27247|url-status=live}}</ref> On December 16, she released an OST for the movie ''[[The Little Prince (2015 film)|The Little Prince]]'' called "Turnaround", along with an accompanying music video.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=117&aid=0002700469|script-title=ko:'어린왕자' 효린 참여 OST, 엔딩크레딧 삽입 '기대↑'|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122248/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=117&aid=0002700469|url-status=live}}</ref>

On March 6, 2016, Hyolyn participated in the singing competition ''[[King of Mask Singer]]'' where she placed second.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2016/03/14/2016031400472.html|script-title=ko:[어저께TV] '복면가왕', 노래·랩 다 잘하는 소리꾼 효린|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002222/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2016/03/14/2016031400472.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2016/03/06/2016030601328.html|script-title=ko:'복면가왕' 봄처녀, 씨스타의 효린일까?...시청자 "목소리톤+특유의 창법 100%"|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=March 7, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160307102236/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2016/03/06/2016030601328.html|url-status=live}}</ref> On June 17, Hyolyn was a contestant on ''[[Duet Song Festival]]'' where she and her partner, Lee Na-hyun, placed second with "Sofa" by R&B singer [[Crush (singer)|Crush]].<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=005&aid=0000910068|script-title=ko:'듀엣가요제' 효린-이나현, 시너지 폭발하며 테이 제치고 1승 차지... '프로들의 만남'|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122229/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=005&aid=0000910068|url-status=live}}</ref> On July 15 Hyolyn released an OST for [[KBS2]]' ''[[Uncontrollably Fond]]'' titled "I Miss You".<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=382&aid=0000488108|script-title=ko:씨스타 효린, '함부로 애틋하게' OST 참여 '보고싶어'|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=August 4, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170804060839/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=382&aid=0000488108|url-status=live}}</ref> On October 21, she featured in a song with [[Far East Movement]] and [[Identity (Far East Movement album)|Gill Chang]] titled, "Umbrella".<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2016/10/20/2016102001015.html|script-title=ko:어반자카파X파 이스트 무브먼트, 정상의 콜라보..21일 공개|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=October 21, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161021122649/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2016/10/20/2016102001015.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2016/10/18/2016101800758.html|script-title=ko:효린X파이스트 무브먼트 '엄브렐라', 프리퀄 영상 공개|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=October 20, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161020071919/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2016/10/18/2016101800758.html|url-status=live}}</ref> After earlier reports that Hyolyn was to release her first EP, an official schedule revealed the release date to be November 8, and also showed features from prominent rapper [[Dok2]] and singer [[Jay Park]] for the tracks "Love Like This" and "One Step" respectively.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://english.yonhapnews.co.kr/search1/2603000000.html?cid=AEN20161017005951315|title=Yonhap News Agency|website=[[Yonhap News Agency]]|language=en|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122222/http://english.yonhapnews.co.kr/search1/2603000000.html?cid=AEN20161017005951315|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://english.yonhapnews.co.kr/search1/2603000000.html?cid=AEN20161026004600315|title=Yonhap News Agency|website=[[Yonhap News Agency]]|language=en|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122235/http://english.yonhapnews.co.kr/search1/2603000000.html?cid=AEN20161026004600315|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=32328|title=Hyolyn to Release Her First Mini Album Tonight|website=BNTNews UK|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209182331/http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=32328|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://thestar.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2016/11/08/2016110800672.html|script-title=ko:씨스타 효린, 타이틀곡 '파라다이스' 공개...실시간 차트 1위|website=thestar.chosun.com|access-date=2018-02-09|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002214/http://thestar.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2016/11/08/2016110800672.html|archive-date=2018-02-10|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=32161|title=Hyolyn Makes Comeback after a 3-year Hiatus|website=BNTNews UK|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209182326/http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=32161|url-status=live}}</ref> The EP, titled ''[[It's Me (EP)|It's Me]]'', was released, with the title track "Paradise" and the accompanying music video.

=== 2017–2019: Collaborations, Sistar's disbandment, and formation of own label ===
Hyolyn participated in the OST for KBS2' ''[[Hwarang: The Poet Warrior Youth]]'' with "Our Tears" ({{Korean|hangul=서로의 눈물이 되어|labels=no}}), released on January 9, 2017.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=015&aid=0003711936|script-title=ko:효린, 월화드라마 '화랑' OST '서로의 눈물이 되어' 10일 공개|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122222/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=015&aid=0003711936|url-status=live}}</ref> On April 14, 2017, Starship Entertainment released a collaboration track featuring Hyolyn and rapper [[Changmo]], titled "Blue Moon", a medium tempo electronic dance track produced by [[Groovy Room]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://thestar.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/04/12/2017041201006.html|script-title=ko:씨스타 효린, 창모와 콜라보 '블루문' 티저 공개 :: THE STAR|website=thestar.chosun.com|access-date=2018-02-09|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002241/http://thestar.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/04/12/2017041201006.html|archive-date=2018-02-10|url-status=dead}}</ref> The track saw success in streaming, digital downloads and, upon its release, hit the upper ranks of several real-time charts including Bugs, Genie and Soribada.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/04/15/2017041500602.html|script-title=ko:효린X창모 '블루문' 음원차트 정상...'원톱과 대세' 시너지|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=April 16, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170416190648/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/04/15/2017041500602.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=241&aid=0002665210|script-title=ko:[차트IS] 효린X창모 '블루문', 4월 3주차 주간차트 1위|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122252/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=241&aid=0002665210|url-status=live}}</ref> It ranked number three on the Gaon Weekly Digital Chart and received nominations for "Best Collaboration" at the 2017 Mnet Asian Music Awards and "Digital Music" division at the 32nd Annual [[Golden Disc Awards|Golden Disk Awards]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.metroseoul.co.kr/news/newsview?newscd=2018011000011|title=[2018 골든디스크] 워너원, BTS, 트와이스...쟁쟁한 후보들 중 대상은?|website=메트로신문|language=ko|access-date=2018-02-09|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209182141/http://www.metroseoul.co.kr/news/newsview?newscd=2018011000011|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://gaonchart.co.kr/main/section/chart/online.gaon?nationGbn=T&serviceGbn=ALL&targetTime=16&hitYear=2017&termGbn=week|script-title=ko:국내 대표 음악 차트 가온차트!|website=[[Gaon Chart]]|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=January 2, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190102193505/http://www.gaonchart.co.kr/main/section/chart/online.gaon?serviceGbn=ALL&termGbn=week&hitYear=2017&targetTime=16&nationGbn=T|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=311&aid=0000785985|script-title=ko:"엑소부터 워너원까지"...2017 MAMA 부문별 후보 공개|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122224/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=311&aid=0000785985|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/10/19/2017101902865.html|script-title=ko:'2017마마', 17개 부문 92팀 후보 발표..워너원·방탄·엑소 3개 후보[종합]|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002243/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/10/19/2017101902865.html|url-status=live}}</ref> After seven years as a group, it was announced on May 23, 2017, that Sistar was to disband.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=109&aid=0003541919|title=[Oh!쎈 초점] 씨스타, 하락세 없던 7년→유독 아쉬운 해체|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122234/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=109&aid=0003541919|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://english.yonhapnews.co.kr/search1/2603000000.html?cid=AEN20170523007300315|title=Sistar to disperse seven years after debut|date=May 22, 2017|website=[[Yonhap News Agency]]|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122231/http://english.yonhapnews.co.kr/search1/2603000000.html?cid=AEN20170523007300315|url-status=live}}</ref> Their final track, titled "Lonely", was released on May 31, rising to the top of the charts and hitting number on the Gaon Weekly Digital Chart.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://gaonchart.co.kr/main/section/chart/online.gaon?nationGbn=T&serviceGbn=ALL&targetTime=22&hitYear=2017&termGbn=week|script-title=ko:국내 대표 음악 차트 가온차트!|website=[[Gaon Chart]]|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=June 11, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170611075851/http://www.gaonchart.co.kr/main/section/chart/online.gaon?nationGbn=T&serviceGbn=ALL&targetTime=22&hitYear=2017&termGbn=week|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|date=June 1, 2017|title=Sistar tops music charts with swansong track|language=en|work=[[The Korea Herald]]|url=http://www.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=20170601000257&ACE_SEARCH=1|access-date=February 8, 2018|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002206/http://www.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=20170601000257&ACE_SEARCH=1|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://thestar.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/05/31/2017053101129.html|script-title=ko:씨스타, 오늘(31일) 굿바이 싱글 'LONELY' 음원 공개 :: THE STAR|website=thestar.chosun.com|access-date=2018-02-09|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002151/http://thestar.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/05/31/2017053101129.html|archive-date=2018-02-10|url-status=dead}}</ref> It was nominated for "Best R&B/Soul Song" at the 2017 [[Melon Music Awards]].<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=081&aid=0002874184|script-title=ko:'오늘 취하면' 수란, '2017 멜론뮤직어워드' GD-자이언티 꺾고 수상|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122241/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=081&aid=0002874184|url-status=live}}</ref> The Groovy Room produced track "Fruity" featuring Hyolyn and [[Kisum]] was released on June 29.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=20170621000691&ACE_SEARCH=1|title=Hyolyn-Kisum releases summer-themed photos|date=June 21, 2017|access-date=2018-02-08|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=33355|title=Hyolyn and Kisum Releases This Summer's Best Hit|website=BNTNews UK|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209182358/http://www.bntnews.co.uk/app/news.php?nid=33355|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/06/27/2017062702190.html|script-title=ko:효린x키썸, 썸머송 '프루티'로 올 여름 달군다|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002204/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/06/27/2017062702190.html|url-status=live}}</ref> On August 25, Hyolyn's OST for [[TVN (South Korea)|tvN]]'s [[Live Up to Your Name|''Live Up To Your Name'']], titled "Always", was released.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/09/27/2017092700726.html|script-title=ko:[공식입장] "민경훈 목소리 저장~"..'명불허전' OST, 정식 발매|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002305/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/09/27/2017092700726.html|url-status=live}}</ref> On September 9, 2017, Hyolyn uploaded a handwritten letter to her personal Instagram account, stating that she had decided to leave Starship Entertainment and would start anew without an agency for the time being.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=023&aid=0003312262|script-title=ko:효린, 7년간 정든 스타쉽 떠나.."정말 오랜 시간 고민을 많이 했다"|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122246/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=023&aid=0003312262|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=082&aid=0000737265|script-title=ko:"혼자 시작하려 한다" 효린, 씨스타 해체 후 행보 자필 편지로 전해|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122236/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=082&aid=0000737265|url-status=live}}</ref> In late 2017, Hyolyn featured in two episodes of the music broadcast ''[[Fantastic Duo|Fantastic Duo 2]]'', competing against [[Jinusean]] and collaborating alongside popular group [[Got7]] with a rendition of her hit track, "Blue Moon".<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/11/10/2017111001839.html|script-title=ko:'판듀2' 효린, 씨스타 해체 후 첫 솔로 무대...여전한 가창력|access-date=2018-02-08|language=ko|archive-date=November 10, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171110082544/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/11/10/2017111001839.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/11/12/2017111201548.html|script-title=ko:'판듀2' 효린 최종 판듀, '신림동 다비드'|access-date=2018-02-08|language=ko|archive-date=November 12, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171112144723/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/11/12/2017111201548.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

[[File:“흰티에 청바지만 걸쳐도” ...효린, 핫한 공항패션 효린 (디패짤) 2.png|thumb|upright=0.8|Hyolyn at Incheon Airport in 2018]]

Not long after Hyolyn announced her departure from Starship Entertainment, she founded her own music label, Bridʒ.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/11/13/2017111300536.html|script-title=ko:[공식]효린, 새 소속사 '브리지' 설립 "다양한 음악 도전할 것"|access-date=2018-02-08|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002206/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/11/13/2017111300536.html|url-status=live}}</ref> She explained in an official statement on November 13, 2017, that the company name, pronounced "Bridge", was meant to symbolize the bridge that she hopes to build between the public and all forms of music production, just how the bridge in a song connects to the song's climax.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/11/13/2017111300587.html|script-title=ko:[공식입장] 씨스타 출신 효린, 소속사 브리지 설립..본격 홀로서기|access-date=2018-02-08|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002218/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2017/11/13/2017111300587.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=241&aid=0002728697|script-title=ko:효린, 홀로서기 시작 "1인 기획사 설립, 다양한 도전"|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122250/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=241&aid=0002728697|url-status=live}}</ref> During the following months, Hyolyn lent her voice to two separate OST tracks; "태업 시계 (Wind Up Watch)" for the drama ''[[Black Knight: The Man Who Guards Me]]'', released on December 20, 2017, and "스쳐간 꿈처럼 (Dreamy Love)" for the drama ''[[Money Flower]]'', released on January 13, 2018.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=108&aid=0002668128|script-title=ko:효린, 씨스타 해체 이후 첫 행보..'흑기사' OST|access-date=2018-02-09|language=ko|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122213/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=108&aid=0002668128|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=20171220000413&ACE_SEARCH=1|title=Hyolyn sings soundtrack for 'Black Knight'|date=December 20, 2017|access-date=2018-02-08|language=en|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002317/http://www.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=20171220000413&ACE_SEARCH=1|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="chosun1">{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2018/01/30/2018013000822.html|script-title=ko:[공식입장] 씨스타 품 벗어난 효린, 첫 솔로 타이틀곡은 '내일할래'|access-date=2018-02-08|language=ko|archive-date=February 10, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002245/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2018/01/30/2018013000822.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Hyolyn officially announced the beginning of her independent work for Bridʒ on January 22, 2018.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://english.yonhapnews.co.kr/search1/2603000000.html?cid=AEN20180122002300315|title=Yonhap News Agency|website=[[Yonhap News Agency]]|language=en|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122228/http://english.yonhapnews.co.kr/search1/2603000000.html?cid=AEN20180122002300315|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://english.yonhapnews.co.kr/search1/2603000000.html?cid=AEN20180201004300315|title=Yonhap News Agency|website=[[Yonhap News Agency]]|language=en|access-date=2018-02-08|archive-date=February 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209122219/http://english.yonhapnews.co.kr/search1/2603000000.html?cid=AEN20180201004300315|url-status=live}}</ref> She announced her plan to unveil a three-part project consisting of three separate singles, starting with her medium tempo, acoustic-pop single "내일할래 (To Do List)", released on February 6, 2018.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2018/02/06/2018020600529.html|script-title=ko:[공식입장] "씨스타→솔로" 효린, 오늘 '내일할래' 발표..직접 프로듀싱|access-date=2018-02-08|language=ko|archive-date=February 6, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180206022102/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2018/02/06/2018020600529.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2018/02/01/2018020101905.html|script-title=ko:효린 "솔로 도전, 힘들지만 견뎌내겠다" 인터뷰 티저 공개|access-date=2018-02-08|language=ko|archive-date=February 1, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180201080600/http://news.chosun.com/site/data/html_dir/2018/02/01/2018020101905.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="chosun1" />

On February 28, Hyolyn featured on [[Got7]]'s pre-release track "너 하나만 (One and Only You)", a single from their later released studio album, ''[[Eyes on You (Got7 EP)|Eyes On You]]''.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://osen.mt.co.kr/article/G1110845144|title=[Oh!쎈 컷] "JB 작사·효린 피처링"...갓세븐, '너 하나만' 스페셜 영상 공개|access-date=2018-04-28|language=ko|archive-date=April 29, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180429093224/http://osen.mt.co.kr/article/G1110845144|url-status=live}}</ref> On April 23, 2018, she revealed the second single from her three-part project, titled "달리 (Dally)", featuring Korean rapper and producer [[Gray (singer)|Gray]]. The song is an upbeat track, styled with [[Contemporary R&B|R&B]]-pop vocals and hip hop percussion. Both Hyolyn and Gray participated in lyrics and production.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.melon.com/album/detail.htm?albumId=10160796|script-title=ko:달리 (Dally) (Feat. GRAY)|website=[[Melon (online music service)|Melon]]|language=ko|access-date=2018-04-28|archive-date=March 16, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210316151138/https://www.melon.com/album/detail.htm?albumId=10160796|url-status=live}}</ref> For the song's accompanying music video, Hyolyn, along with four other dancers, performed choreography by American choreographer Aliya Janell. The music video garnered over one million views in less than 24 hours of release.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=312&aid=0000325247|script-title=ko:효린, 오늘(23일) 싱글 '달리' 공개(feat.그레이)|access-date=2018-04-28|language=ko|archive-date=April 29, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180429092726/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=312&aid=0000325247|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=410&aid=0000463919|script-title=ko:효린 '달리' 19금 안무, 맹연습으로 단련된 퍼포먼스|access-date=2018-04-28|language=ko|archive-date=April 29, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180429092504/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=410&aid=0000463919|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=382&aid=0000641177|script-title=ko:효린 '달리' M/V 유튜브 조회수 100만뷰 돌파|access-date=2018-04-28|language=ko|archive-date=April 29, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180429155040/http://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=382&aid=0000641177|url-status=live}}</ref> The last single for her three-part project, titled "바다보러갈래 (See Sea)", was released on July 19, 2018.<ref>{{Cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/hyolyn-see-sea-world-digital-song-sales-chart/|title=Hyolyn Earns Highest Solo Entry to Date on World Digital Song Sales With 'See Sea'|last=Benjamin|first=Jeff|date=August 1, 2018|magazine=Billboard|access-date=2019-05-22|archive-date=August 9, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180809043913/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/k-town/8468223/hyolyn-see-sea-world-digital-song-sales-chart|url-status=live}}</ref> Her next single, "BAE", was released on August 14, 2018.<ref>{{Cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/hyolyn-summertime-anthem-bae-video-8470669/|title=Hyolyn Delivers Summertime Anthem In 'Bae' Music Video: Watch|last=Benjamin|first=Jeff|date=August 17, 2018|magazine=Billboard|access-date=2019-05-22|archive-date=August 23, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180823172449/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/k-town/8470669/hyolyn-summertime-anthem-bae-video|url-status=live}}</ref> Hyolyn collaborated with [[Melanie Fontana]] on the single titled "니가 더 잘 알잖아 (youknowbetter)", which was released on May 22, 2019.<ref name="Hyolyn unveils new project for comeback">{{Cite web|url=https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/www/art/2019/05/682_268462.html|title=Hyolyn unveils new project for comeback|last=Lee|first=Gyu-lee|date=May 7, 2019|website=[[The Korea Times]]|access-date=2019-05-22|archive-date=May 11, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190511065510/http://www.koreatimes.co.kr/www/art/2019/05/682_268462.html|url-status=live}}</ref> She began her first solo world tour "2019 Hyolyn 1st World Tour [TRUE]," in Berlin, May 29. The tour will run from Europe, the Middle East to Asia, ending with a concert in Tokyo on June 30.<ref name="Hyolyn unveils new project for comeback" />

=== 2020–present: ''Say My Name'', ''QueenDom'', ''Ice'', and solo concerts ===
On August 19, 2020, Hyolyn released her second EP ''[[Say My Name (Hyolyn EP)|Say My Name]]'', with the title track of the same name. The album features the song "9Lives", an autobiographical song, that's performance was praised for its artistic expression of the story.<ref>{{Cite web|date=August 29, 2020|script-title=ko:'음악중심' 효린, '9LIVES' 무대 '감동 퍼포먼스'|url=https://www.hankookilbo.com/News/Read/A2020082922020004687?t=20200906000524|access-date=2020-09-06|website=[[Hankook Ilbo]]|language=ko|archive-date=July 27, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210727075511/https://www.hankookilbo.com/News/Read/A2020082922020004687?t=20200906000524|url-status=live}}</ref> ''Say My Name'' also includes the previously released singles "Dally", "See Sea" and "BAE".<ref>{{Cite web|last=김 |first=효정|date=August 18, 2020|script-title=ko:효린, 19일 미니 2집으로 컴백...직접 프로듀싱|url=https://www.yna.co.kr/view/AKR20200818041400005|access-date=2020-09-06|website=[[Yonhap News Agency]]|language=ko|archive-date=July 27, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210727075511/https://www.yna.co.kr/view/AKR20200818041400005|url-status=live}}</ref>

