'''Kang Ji-hyun''' ({{Korean|강지현}}; born February 12, 1992),<ref name="dob1" /><ref name="dob2" /><ref name="dob3" /> known professionally as '''Soyou''' ({{Korean|labels=no|소유}}), is a South Korean singer. She is best known as a former member of the South Korean girl group [[Sistar]].

==Early life and education==
Soyou was born on February 12, 1992,<ref name="dob1">{{cite book|author=Mark Russell|title=K-Pop Now!: The Korean Music Revolution|page=100|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=etDZAwAAQBAJ|date=April 29, 2014|publisher=Tuttle Publishing|isbn=978-1-4629-1411-1}}</ref><ref name="dob2">{{Cite web|script-title=ko:씨스타 {{!}} My name is...1|trans-title=Sistar {{!}} My name is ...1|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/home/article/312/0000004967|via=[[Naver]]|work=[[Ten Asia]]|language=ko|last=Lee|first=Seung-han|date=October 19, 2010|access-date=September 13, 2025|archive-date=September 13, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913144314/https://m.entertain.naver.com/home/article/312/0000004967|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="dob3">{{Cite web|script-title=ko:씨스타 소유, 애교 셀카로 근황 인사 "생일 축하 고마워"|trans-title=SISTAR's Soyou shares her latest update with a cute selfie: "Thank you for the birthday wishes"|url=https://tvdaily.co.kr/read.php3?aid=14552355091070916017|website=TV Daily|language=ko|last=Lee|first=Hye-rin|date=February 12, 2016|access-date=September 13, 2025|archive-date=September 13, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913144317/https://tvdaily.co.kr/read.php3?aid=14552355091070916017|url-status=live}}</ref> in [[Jeju Island]], South Korea. Before debuting, she was a licensed hairdresser and worked in a hair salon.<ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:씨스타 소유 "밥 먹고 살려고 미용 자격증 땄다"|url=https://sports.donga.com/3/all/20160623/78835014/1|website=Sports Dong-a|language=ko|date=June 23, 2016|access-date=August 12, 2020|archive-date=October 6, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211006070337/https://sports.donga.com/3/all/20160623/78835014/1|url-status=live}}</ref> Soyou was known as a [[Cube Entertainment]] trainee, who was originally supposed to debut as a member of [[4Minute]].<ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:씨스타 보라 "포미닛과 경쟁구도, 정말 싫었다"|url=http://mosen.mt.co.kr/article/G1109443698|website=mosen.mt.co.kr|language=ko|last=OSEN|date=August 1, 2012|access-date=August 12, 2020|archive-date=October 6, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211006070336/http://mosen.mt.co.kr/article/G1109443698|url-status=live}}</ref> Soyou has said that she didn't make it into the group because she was lacking in many ways and was originally supposed to be in [[Kwon So-hyun|Sohyun]]'s place.<ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:'놀러와' 소현 "원래 씨스타의 소유가 포미닛 멤버"|url=http://mosen.mt.co.kr/article/G1109374976|website=mosen.mt.co.kr|language=ko|last=OSEN|date=April 2, 2012|access-date=August 13, 2020|archive-date=October 6, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211006070338/http://mosen.mt.co.kr/article/G1109374976|url-status=live}}</ref>  Instead, Soyou auditioned for [[Starship Entertainment]], singing a cover of Navi's "On The Road", and after her traineeship, she debuted as a member of [[Sistar]] in June 2010.<ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:소유, 오디션 때 부른 '길에서' 다시 부른다... 적재와 협업|url=https://www.yna.co.kr/view/AKR20191223049800005|website=[[Yonhap News Agency]]|language=ko|last=오|first=보람|date=December 23, 2019|access-date=August 13, 2020|archive-date=October 6, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211006070337/https://www.yna.co.kr/view/AKR20191223049800005|url-status=live}}</ref> The group gained significant popularity after the release of their hit single "So Cool" in 2011.<ref>[https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/467764/billboard-k-pop-hot-100-launches-sistar-is-no-1-on-new-korea-chart "Billboard K-Pop Hot 100 Launches; SISTAR Is No. 1 on New Korea Chart"] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190710051804/https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/467764/billboard-k-pop-hot-100-launches-sistar-is-no-1-on-new-korea-chart |date=July 10, 2019 }}, ''[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]'', August 25, 2011. Retrieved August 12, 2020.</ref>

Soyou pursued her middle school at Mullae Middle School and completed high school at the [[Korean Arts High School]] with a specialization in [[theater]] and [[film]].<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:한국예술학교, LBMA STAR 유치... 차세대 키즈 스타 발굴 앞장서|url=https://www.bntnews.co.kr/article/view/bnt202006290002|website=Bnt News|last=Lee|first=Sa-bae|access-date=March 31, 2024|archive-date=September 13, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913144713/https://www.bntnews.co.kr/article/view/bnt202006290002|url-status=live}}</ref> In 2012, she earned her Bachelor of Arts in Contemporary Applied Music degree from [[Sungshin Women's University]].<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:씨스타 효린·소유, 성신여대 입학홍보 나서|url=https://n.news.naver.com/article/277/0003395556?sid=102|website=[[Naver]]|publisher=AsiaE|last=Oh|first=Jin-hee|access-date=March 31, 2024|archive-date=September 13, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913144716/https://n.news.naver.com/article/277/0003395556?sid=102|url-status=live}}</ref>

==Career==
===2010–2017: Original soundtracks, collaborations and Sistar disbandment===
{{Main article|Sistar}}
In August 2010, Soyou collaborated with Kan Jongwoo of J2 for the soundtrack for the drama ''Gloria''. In September, she also sang a soundtrack for [[Munhwa Broadcasting Corporation|MBC]]'s drama ''[[Playful Kiss]]''. The song is titled "Should I Confess".<ref>{{cite web|title=SISTAR's Soyu sings for 'Playful Kiss' OST|url=http://www.allkpop.com/2010/09/sistars-soyu-sings-for-playful-kiss-ost|publisher=[[Allkpop]]|access-date=January 6, 2015|archive-date=February 5, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120205202001/http://www.allkpop.com/2010/09/sistars-soyu-sings-for-playful-kiss-ost|url-status=live}}</ref>{{Unreliable source|reason=Per [[WP:KO/RS#UR]]|date=February 2025}}

In November 2012, Soyou sang a duet with hip-hop duo Geeks. The song "Officially Missing You, Too" is a remake of Tamia's song of the same title. It is a part of Geeks' project album, ''Re;Code Episode 1''.<ref>{{cite web|title=[Video] SISTAR's Soyou and Geeks Release 'Officially Missing You, Too' MV|url=http://sg.entertainment.yahoo.com/news/video-sistar-s-soyou-and-geeks-release-officially-045506888.html|work=Yahoo Entertainment Singapore|date=November 1, 2012|access-date=January 6, 2015|archive-date=October 25, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141025214433/https://sg.entertainment.yahoo.com/news/video-sistar-s-soyou-and-geeks-release-officially-045506888.html|url-status=live}}</ref> She also collaborated with fellow label mates, [[K.Will]] and [[Boyfriend (band)|Boyfriend]]'s Jeongmin, for Starship Planet's yearly holiday release, titled "White Love".<ref>{{cite web|title=K.Will, SISTAR's Soyu, & Boyfriend's Jeongmin release "White Love" MV|url=http://www.allkpop.com/2012/11/k-will-sistars-soyu-release-white-love-mv-starring-boyfriends-jeongmin-k-pop-stars-huh-ji-won|publisher=[[Allkpop]]|access-date=January 6, 2015|archive-date=May 15, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130515082340/http://www.allkpop.com/2012/11/k-will-sistars-soyu-release-white-love-mv-starring-boyfriends-jeongmin-k-pop-stars-huh-ji-won|url-status=live}}</ref>{{Unreliable source|reason=Per [[WP:KO/RS#UR]]|date=February 2025}}

[[File:Soyou at Golden Disk Awards Red Carpet in 2013.jpg|thumb|left|upright|Soyou at the [[27th Golden Disc Awards]]]]

In September 2013, it was revealed that Soyou and [[Mad Clown]] would release a duet called "[[Stupid in Love (Soyou & Mad Clown song)|Stupid in Love]]" on the 10th.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Mad Clown seriously hits the charts|url=https://www.koreajoongangdaily.com/korea/mad-clown-seriously-hits-the-charts/10603620|website=[[Korea JoongAng Daily]]|language=en|date=April 6, 2014|access-date=August 13, 2020|archive-date=May 6, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210506225857/https://koreajoongangdaily.joins.com/2014/04/06/etc/Mad-Clown-seriously-hits-the-charts/2987474.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

In February 2014, Soyou and [[Junggigo]] released a duet called "[[Some (song)|Some]]".<ref>{{cite web|title=SISTAR's Soyu and hip hop vocal JungGiGo form a duet unit!|url=http://www.allkpop.com/article/2014/02/sistars-soyu-and-hip-hop-vocal-junggigo-form-a-duet-unit|publisher=[[Allkpop]]|access-date=January 6, 2015|archive-date=January 9, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150109131013/http://www.allkpop.com/article/2014/02/sistars-soyu-and-hip-hop-vocal-junggigo-form-a-duet-unit|url-status=live}}</ref>{{Unreliable source|reason=Per [[WP:KO/RS#UR]]|date=February 2025}}

In January 2015, it was revealed that Soyou, together with [[Lee Hanee]] and Kim Jungmin, would be the new MCs of beauty tip program ''Get It Beauty''. The new MCs' first episode aired on February 4, 2015.<ref>{{cite web|title=Honey Lee, Sistar's Soyu, and Kim Jung Min to Be New MC's of "Get It Beauty 2015" – Soompi|url=http://www.soompi.com/2015/01/04/honey-lee-sistars-soyu-and-kim-jung-min-to-be-new-mcs-of-get-it-beauty-2015/|work=[[Soompi]]|date=January 5, 2015|access-date=January 6, 2015|archive-date=January 5, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150105113308/http://www.soompi.com/2015/01/04/honey-lee-sistars-soyu-and-kim-jung-min-to-be-new-mcs-of-get-it-beauty-2015/|url-status=live}}</ref>{{Unreliable source|reason=Per [[WP:KO/RS#UR]]|date=February 2025}}

[[File:씨스타(SISTAR) G페스티벌 아시아 드림 콘서트 (2).jpg|thumb|upright|Soyou performing in 2016]]

In February 2017, Soyou and [[Byun Baek-hyun|Baekhyun]] released a duet called "[[Rain (Soyou and Baekhyun song)|Rain]]".<ref>{{Cite news|script-title=ko:소유X백현, 역대급 듀엣곡 탄생될까 "2월 중 공개"|url=https://www.heraldmuse.com/article/1229717|work=Herald Muse|language=ko|last=박|first=수정|date=February 6, 2017|access-date=February 6, 2017|archive-date=April 7, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190407030112/http://pop.heraldcorp.com/view.php?ud=201702061441195508678_1|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|script-title=ko:"최강 듀엣"...소유X백현 콜라보, 14일 발매 확정|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/home/article/109/0003474429|work=Osen|via=Naver|access-date=February 7, 2017|archive-date=April 7, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190407070114/https://m.entertain.naver.com/read?oid=109&aid=0003474429|url-status=live}}</ref>

In May 2017, Sistar released their last single "Lonely".<ref>{{cite web|title=Sistar to disperse seven years after debut|url=http://english.yonhapnews.co.kr/news/2017/05/23/49/0200000000AEN20170523007351315F.html|website=[[Yonhap News Agency]]|date=May 22, 2017|access-date=November 30, 2017|archive-date=June 3, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170603154358/http://english.yonhapnews.co.kr/news/2017/05/23/49/0200000000AEN20170523007351315F.html|url-status=live}}</ref> The group performed their most successful summer hits – "Touch My Body", "Shake It", "Loving U", "I Swear" and also their last song "Lonely" on four major music shows, before concluding the schedule on ''[[Inkigayo]]'' on June 4, 2017 and officially disbanding.<ref>{{cite web|title=Starship Entertainment Reveals Real Reason Why SISTAR Disbanded; Girls Say Reunion Is Possible|url=http://en.koreaportal.com/articles/37161/20170606/starship-entertainment-reveals-real-reason-why-sistar-disbanded-girls-reunion.htm|publisher=Korea Portal|date=June 6, 2017|access-date=November 30, 2017|archive-date=June 9, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170609060624/http://en.koreaportal.com/articles/37161/20170606/starship-entertainment-reveals-real-reason-why-sistar-disbanded-girls-reunion.htm|url-status=live}}</ref>{{Unreliable source|reason=Per [[WP:KO/RS#UR]]|date=February 2025}}

In August 2017, Soyou was featured as the vocalist on Primary's song "Right?".<ref>{{cite web|title=Primary reveals 'Right?' feat. Soyu MV + 'Pop' collab MVs with Solji, JB, Sunggyu, Sandeul, & Yoseob|url=https://www.allkpop.com/article/2017/08/primary-reveals-right-feat-soyu-mv-pop-collab-mvs-with-solji-jb-sunggyu-sandeul-yoseob|publisher=[[Allkpop]]|date=August 30, 2017|access-date=November 30, 2017|archive-date=January 5, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180105224020/https://www.allkpop.com/article/2017/08/primary-reveals-right-feat-soyu-mv-pop-collab-mvs-with-solji-jb-sunggyu-sandeul-yoseob|url-status=live}}</ref>{{Unreliable source|reason=Per [[WP:KO/RS#UR]]|date=February 2025}}

===2017–2023: Solo debut===
{{Main|Re:Born (EP)|Re:Fresh (EP)}}
After Sistar disbanded in June 2017, Soyou debuted her solo career under Starship Entertainment.<ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:씨스타 내려놓은 소유, 이토록 성공적인 솔로 신고식|url=https://www.newsen.com/news_view.php?uid=201712180905470410|website=Newsen|date=December 18, 2017|access-date=September 5, 2020|archive-date=May 14, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210514091456/https://www.newsen.com/news_view.php?uid=201712180905470410|url-status=live}}</ref> She was featured on K.Will's fourth album ''Part.1 Nonfiction,'' for the B-side track titled "Let Me Hear You Say", released on September 26.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:스타쉽 측 "소유, 케이윌 새 앨범 수록곡 피처링 참여"|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/home/article/109/0003622754|work=Osen|via=Naver|access-date=August 13, 2020|archive-date=July 30, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230730173311/https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/now/article/109/0003622754|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:[단독] "스타쉽 감성보컬"...소유, 케이윌 신곡 피처링 지원사격|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/home/article/311/0000776794|work=Xports News|via=Naver|access-date=August 13, 2020|archive-date=July 7, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180707005900/https://m.entertain.naver.com/read?oid=311&aid=0000776794|url-status=live}}</ref> She released a collaboration track titled "Monitor Girl" with Geeks' Louie on October 26, it was their second collaboration since "Officially Missing You, Too" in 2012.<ref>{{cite web|title=Watch: Soyou and Geeks's Louie Drop MV for Collaboration Track "Monitor Girl"|url=https://www.soompi.com/2017/10/25/watch-soyou-geekss-louie-drop-mv-collaboration-track-monitor-girl/|date=October 25, 2017|access-date=November 30, 2017|archive-date=December 1, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171201033337/https://www.soompi.com/2017/10/25/watch-soyou-geekss-louie-drop-mv-collaboration-track-monitor-girl/|url-status=live}}</ref>{{Unreliable source|reason=Per [[WP:KO/RS#UR]]|date=February 2025}} On November 16, Soyou released "I Still" with [[Sung Si-kyung]] as pre-release track for her upcoming solo album.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:[공식] 소유 측 "11월 컴백 준비 중...성시경 지원사격"|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/home/article/311/0000787716|work=Xports News|via=Naver|access-date=August 13, 2020|archive-date=July 7, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180707010013/https://m.entertain.naver.com/read?oid=311&aid=0000787716|url-status=live}}</ref> On November 28, Soyou was confirmed to become an MC for a new beauty program of JTBC titled SoyouXHani's Beauty View, which began airing on December 28.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:[단독] 소유X하니, 이름 걸고 새 뷰티프로 론칭..12월 첫방송|url=http://mosen.mt.co.kr/article/G1110785340|website=Osen|date=November 28, 2017|access-date=August 13, 2020|archive-date=October 6, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211006070327/http://mosen.mt.co.kr/article/G1110785340|url-status=live}}</ref> On December 13, Soyou released the first part of her solo album titled ''Re:Born'' with the single "The Night" featuring rapper duo [[Geeks (musical duo)|Geeks]] and produced by Primary.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:[한국언론의 세대교체 ◆브레이크뉴스◆] '리:본(Re:born)' 컴백 소유, 호흡 빼고 공감 더하고.."믿고 듣는 가수 되고파"|url=http://m.breaknews.com/a.html?uid=547993&section=sc4|date=December 13, 2017|access-date=December 25, 2017|archive-date=April 22, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220422024325/http://m.breaknews.com/a.html?uid=547993&section=sc4|url-status=dead}}</ref>

A year and nine months after her last release, Soyou released "Gotta Go" on June 28, 2020.<ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:소유 소감, "'가라고' 활동, 짧았지만 힘 많이 났다"|url=http://daily.hankooki.com/lpage/entv/202008/dh20200824083259139020.htm|website=daily.hankooki.com|language=ko|date=August 24, 2020|access-date=August 27, 2020|archive-date=April 18, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210418044250/http://daily.hankooki.com/lpage/entv/202008/dh20200824083259139020.htm|url-status=live}}</ref> The song is a reggaeton, dance hall style song and was accompanied by a music video, released through Starship Entertainment's YouTube channel.<ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:'원조 썸머퀸' 소유, 오늘(30일) '엠카' 컴백...신곡 '가라고' 무대 최초 공개|url=https://www.hankyung.com/entertainment/article/202007305042I|website=[[The Korea Economic Daily]]|language=ko|date=July 30, 2020|access-date=August 27, 2020|archive-date=September 21, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200921140545/https://www.hankyung.com/entertainment/article/202007305042I|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|script-title=ko:소유, 신곡 '가라고' 안무 영상 공개...탄탄한 건강미|url=https://www.news1.kr/articles/?4016979|website=뉴스1|language=ko|date=August 5, 2020|access-date=August 27, 2020|archive-date=October 6, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211006070327/https://www.news1.kr/articles/?4016979|url-status=live}}</ref>

After eight months, Starship Entertainment announced that Soyou is gearing up for her next comeback on March 11, 2021. Soyou's new single "Good Night My Love" was reportedly written by [[Lee Hyori]] and composed by [[Babylon (singer)|Babylon]].<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:소유, 이효리 작사·베이빌론 작곡 신곡으로 11일 컴백[공식입장]|url=https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/article/311/0001270467?lfrom=twitter|date=March 3, 2021|access-date=March 3, 2021|archive-date=March 3, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210303023139/https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/article/311/0001270467?lfrom=twitter|url-status=live}}</ref>

On September 8, Soyou decided not to renew her contract with Starship Entertainment.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:소유, 11년 만 스타쉽과 이별.."재계약 체결 NO, 새출발 응원"[전문](공식)|trans-title=Soyou, farewell from Starship after 11 years.."No contract renewal, support for a new start"[Full text](Official)|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/now/article/112/0003474785|via=[[Naver]]|work=Herald Muse|language=ko|last=Park|first=Seo-yeon|date=September 8, 2021|access-date=September 8, 2021|archive-date=September 8, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210908084157/https://entertain.naver.com/now/read?oid=112&aid=0003474785|url-status=live}}</ref>  Later on September 29, Soyou signed with [[BPM Entertainment]].<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:소유, 신생 엔터사 빅플래닛메이드와 전속계약 체결 [공식]|trans-title=Soyou signs exclusive contract with Big Planet Made, a new entertainment company [Official]|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/now/article/108/0002992155|via=[[Naver]]|work=Star News|language=ko|last=Lee|first=Deok-haeng|date=September 29, 2021|access-date=September 29, 2021|archive-date=September 29, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210929042729/https://entertain.naver.com/now/read?oid=108&aid=0002992155|url-status=live}}</ref>

On March 1, 2022, BPM Entertainment announced Soyou would hold her first solo concert 'THE LIVE: NIGHT' on April 2 and 3.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:소유, 데뷔 첫 단독 콘서트 개최...4월 열린다 [공식]|trans-title=Soyou held her first solo concert since her debut... Open in April [Official]|url=https://entertain.naver.com/now/read?oid=117&aid=0003581035|via=[[Naver]]|work=My Daily|language=ko|last=Oh|first=Yoon-joo|date=March 2, 2022|access-date=March 2, 2022|archive-date=March 2, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220302064206/https://entertain.naver.com/now/read?oid=117&aid=0003581035|url-status=live}}</ref> On April 27, Soyou released her third EP ''Day & Night'', with the lead single "Business", featuring [[Be'O]].<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:소유, 27일 새 미니음반 발표...소속사 이적 후 첫 앨범|trans-title=Soyou releases a new mini album on the 27th... The first album after moving to the agency|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/now/article/001/0013127787|via=[[Naver]]|work=[[Yonhap News Agency]]|language=ko|last=Lee|first=Tae-soo|date=April 21, 2022|access-date=April 21, 2022|archive-date=April 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220421001305/https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/now/article/001/0013127787|url-status=live}}</ref>

===2024–present: Business venture===

On July 31, Soyou established the corporation So & You, wherein she was able to launch in November the whiskey-based "So Whiskey Highball" and the high-alcohol-based "So Goryangju Highball" in cans.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:BTS 진도 나섰다...'박재범·성시경·소유' 연예인 주류 전성시대 활짝|trans-title=BTS has stepped up... 'Jay Park, Sung Si Kyung, Soyou' Celebrity Mainstream Heyday in Full Swing|url=https://n.news.naver.com/article/421/0007959760?sid=101|via=[[Naver]]|work=News1|language=ko|last=Bae|first=Ji-yoon|date=December 11, 2024|access-date=December 14, 2024|archive-date=September 13, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913144719/https://n.news.naver.com/article/421/0007959760?sid=101|url-status=live}}</ref>

==Other ventures==
===Ambassadorship===

In July 2014, Soyou became the promotional ambassador for the [[JTBC Seoul Marathon]] event, attended by 20,000 participants. Chosen by the event coordinator, Soyou's passion for running and commitment to self-care through exercise resonated with the event's theme, "Run As I Am."<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:소유, JTBC 서울마라톤 홍보대사 선정|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/home/article/001/0010268347|via=Naver|work=[[Yonhap News Agency]]|last=Lee|first=Jeong-hyeon|date=September 14, 2018|access-date=March 21, 2024|archive-date=March 21, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240321081824/https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/article/001/0010268347|url-status=live}}</ref>

In September 2018, Soyou became the public relations ambassador for the [[Seoul]] branch of the [[Korean Red Cross]], appointed by its Chairman. She has been supporting the Seoul branch since 2015, aiding underprivileged groups like undernourished children, child-headed households, elderly individuals living alone, and multicultural families.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:소유, 어머니와의 인연으로 대한적십자사 서울특별시지사 홍보대사 위촉|url=https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/article/144/0000576915|website=Sports Khan|publisher=[[Naver]]|last=Ha|first=Kyung-hyeon|date=October 11, 2018|access-date=March 21, 2024|archive-date=March 21, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240321082819/https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/article/144/0000576915|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Endorsements===

In September 2014, Soyou collaborated with the "비커즈 (bcuz)" brand, known for its "wrap jeans," a popular fashion item at the time.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:씨스타 소유, 청바지 화보로 '명품 각선미' 과시...'완벽' 바디라인|url=https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/article/030/0002306060|work=Etnews|via=[[Naver]]|last=Shin|first=Ji-hye|date=September 24, 2014|access-date=March 21, 2024|archive-date=March 21, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240321144527/https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/article/030/0002306060|url-status=live}}</ref> She continued her promotions with the brand, which had become a household name for its sportswear, by introducing and releasing new products for its 2015 S/S season.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:씨스타, 효린-소유 완벽 몸매 화보 공개|url=https://n.news.naver.com/article/005/0000747487?sid=103|website=Kmib|publisher=[[Naver]]|last=Lee|first=Gwang-hyeong|date=March 10, 2015|access-date=March 21, 2024|archive-date=March 21, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240321145827/https://n.news.naver.com/article/005/0000747487?sid=103|url-status=live}}</ref> In June 2015, Soyou teamed up with [[Sung Si-kyung]] as endorsers for [[CJ CheilJedang]]'s 'Bibigo Wanggyoja,' a side dish ideal for pairing with beer. The duo filmed TV commercials and advertisements together.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:CJ제일제당, '바삭∼ 아삭∼' 왕교자, 맥주와 찰떡궁합이네!|url=https://n.news.naver.com/article/020/0002804891?sid=103|website=[[The Dong-A Ilbo]]|publisher=[[Naver]]|last=|first=|date=June 10, 2015|access-date=March 21, 2024|archive-date=March 21, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240321151547/https://n.news.naver.com/article/020/0002804891?sid=103|url-status=live}}</ref>

In July 2017, she was chosen as a model for GRN's health supplement products. She specifically endorsed well-known celebrity diet products such as Green Tea Catechins and Mister Red Power Up.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:건강한 걸그룹 몸매 소유, 다이어트 브랜드GRN 모델 계약|url=https://www.cctvnews.co.kr/news/articleView.html?idxno=69538|website=CCTV|publisher=[[Naver]]|last=Lee|first=Yoo-jeong|date=July 10, 2017|access-date=March 21, 2024|archive-date=March 21, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240321152900/https://www.cctvnews.co.kr/news/articleView.html?idxno=69538|url-status=live}}</ref> In the following years, Soyou continued promoting the brand, later adding their anti-aging supplement products to her list of endorsements, before parting ways at the end of 2021.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:현아와 소유가 선택한 몸매관리 grn 관리법|url=https://www.it-b.co.kr/news/articleView.html?idxno=23996|website=CCTV|publisher=[[Naver]]|last=Lee|first=Jeong-gil|date=September 4, 2018|access-date=March 21, 2024|archive-date=March 21, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240321153919/https://www.it-b.co.kr/news/articleView.html?idxno=23996|url-status=live}}</ref> Later in 2017, Soyou, a singer born in [[Jeju Province|Jeju]], was selected by [[Emart|E'Mart]] as their endorser for their new liquor product called "Blue Night," which originated from Jeju. As part of the promotion, she released the single "Blue Nights of Jeju Island" alongside commercials and remained an active endorser until 2019.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:이마트, '푸른밤'으로 몽골서 소주한류 개척한다|url=https://n.news.naver.com/article/016/0001304900?sid=101|work=Heraldbiz|via=[[Naver]]|last=Kim|first=Seong-woo|date=October 23, 2017|access-date=March 21, 2024|archive-date=March 21, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240321160631/https://n.news.naver.com/article/016/0001304900?sid=101|url-status=live}}</ref>

In September 2018, she participated as an endorser in [[Lotte Corporation|Lotte Rental]]'s summer vacation season exhibition for their lifestyle platform "MYOMEE." The platform allows users to rent a variety of products and goods necessary for traveling through their app for a reasonable period of time.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:여름휴가철 한때 뿐인 바캉스상품, '묘미'로 빌리자|url=https://m.ajunews.com/view/20180718093825432|website=Ajunews|publisher=[[Naver]]|last=Sun|first=Seuk-yu|date=July 18, 2018|access-date=March 21, 2024|archive-date=March 21, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240321161650/https://m.ajunews.com/view/20180718093825432#_mobwcvr|url-status=live}}</ref>

In May 2020, the food corporation "Cookat" launched their new PB (Private Brand) products, 'Mukbang Tteokbokki Chicken Feet' and 'Grilled Chicken Tail Bones.' The launch is in collaboration with Soyou, who is one of the entertainment industry's leading 'chicken feet enthusiasts'. Soyou participated in the entire product development process such as recipe development, package design, and product capacity setting.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:쿠캣, 가수 소유와 콜라보로 '소유하고 싶은 안주' 2종 출시|url=https://n.news.naver.com/article/076/0003563012?sid=101|website=[[Sports Chosun]]|publisher=[[Naver]]|last=Lee|first=Jeong-hyuk|date=May 6, 2020|access-date=March 23, 2024|archive-date=March 23, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240323013637/https://n.news.naver.com/article/076/0003563012?sid=101|url-status=live}}</ref> In March 2021, Soyou, alongside [[Iz*One]], was selected as [[Pepsi Zero Sugar]]'s 2021 K-POP partners, releasing the single 'ZERO: ATTITUDE' as part of the 'Pepsi 2021 K-POP Campaign.'<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:"아이즈원·소유의 매력"...롯데칠성음료 '펩시 제로 슈거' 라임향 광고 온에어|url=https://www.youthdaily.co.kr/mobile/article.html?no=64617|website=Youth Daily|last=Kim|first=Lee-na|date=March 9, 2021|access-date=March 23, 2024|archive-date=March 23, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240323014755/https://www.youthdaily.co.kr/mobile/article.html?no=64617|url-status=live}}</ref>

Later in August 2021, Soyou, along with comedian [[Yoo Se-yoon]], was selected as an endorser for the 'healthy active vacation' campaign by Frip, a tourism venture founded by the [[Korea Tourism Organization]].<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:소유·유세윤 '건강한 바캉스' 모델 됐다...관광벤처 프립 진행|url=https://n.news.naver.com/article/016/0001872017?sid=103|work=Herald Biz|via=[[Naver]]|last=Ham|first=Young-hoon|date=August 9, 2021|access-date=March 23, 2024|archive-date=March 23, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240323020716/https://n.news.naver.com/article/016/0001872017?sid=103|url-status=live}}</ref> In September 2023, Saint Satin selected Soyou as the brand's exclusive model for their Fret Acupressure Slippers, which can be worn all year round, and Fret's Indoor shoes that prevent noise between floors.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:세인트새틴, 프렛지압슬리퍼 전속 모델로 가수 소유 발탁|url=http://m.beyondpost.co.kr/view.php?ud=2023092010303782966cf2d78c68_30|website=Beyond Post|publisher=[[Naver]]|last=Kim|first=Min-hyuk|date=September 20, 2023|access-date=March 24, 2024|archive-date=March 24, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324031122/http://m.beyondpost.co.kr/view.php?ud=2023092010303782966cf2d78c68_30|url-status=live}}</ref>

In March 2024, Soyou filmed commercials promoting the beverage 'Refreshingly Empty Barrel Light' (hereinafter referred to as Barrel Light) by Donghwa Pharmaceutical, a functional beverage product for constipation.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:동화약품 '배러라이트&배러화이트' 모델에 소유·다솜 선정|url=https://www.kpanews.co.kr/article/show.asp?idx=249165&category=D|website=kpanews.co.kr|publisher=[[Naver]]|last=Lee|first=Jong-tae|date=March 8, 2024|access-date=December 14, 2024|archive-date=September 13, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913144829/https://www.kpanews.co.kr/article/show.asp?idx=249165&category=D|url-status=live}}</ref> In May, Soyou was selected by BlingU Co., Ltd. as the endorser of their "calf and shoulder massager" product, which was first introduced by the home appliance brand "Iyuz" and has been the top pick in the Korean Consumer Preferred Brands of small massagers.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:'이유즈종이리,어깨마사지기'이유즈 안마기, 2관왕 수상|url=https://www.bizwnews.com/news/articleView.html?idxno=81940|website=Bizwnews|publisher=[[Naver]]|last=Kim|first=Eun-ah|date=May 3, 2024|access-date=December 14, 2024|archive-date=September 13, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913144830/https://www.bizwnews.com/news/articleView.html?idxno=81940|url-status=live}}</ref> In October 2024, Soyou endorsed the "30-Second Quick Bubble Mask" product by the skincare brand "Menokin," a brand that has grown more than three times since its launch in 2023.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:메노킨(MENOKIN), 소유와 함께 마스크팩'30초팩 레이어링' 캠 페인 공개|url=https://www.enetnews.co.kr/news/articleView.html?idxno=29857|website=Enet News|publisher=[[Naver]]|last=Kim|first=Ji-won|date=October 2, 2024|access-date=December 14, 2024|archive-date=September 13, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913144933/https://www.enetnews.co.kr/news/articleView.html?idxno=29857|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Philanthropy===

In May 2017, Soyou donated {{KRW|10|link=yes}} million won to the [[Korean Red Cross]] to support the underprivileged. On the same day, the organization revealed that she had been a part of the "Philanthropy and Culture Committee" of the Seoul branch since 2015, a group composed solely of high-value donors.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:씨스타 소유, 참 꾸준한 선행... 적십자에 1천만원 또 기부|trans-title=SISTAR's Soyou, truly consistent good deeds... Donated another 10 million won to the Red Cross|url=https://n.news.naver.com/mnews/article/005/0000991238?sid=102|via=[[Naver]]|work=Kookmin Ilbo|language=ko|last=Kim|first=Dong-woon|date=May 13, 2017|access-date=March 24, 2024|archive-date=March 24, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324032355/https://n.news.naver.com/mnews/article/005/0000991238?sid=102|url-status=live}}</ref> In the following year, she was recognized as part of their 'Seoul Red Cross Pine Tree Club,' which is composed of individuals with cumulative donations totaling more than {{KRW|30|link=yes}} million won.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:소유, 고액기부자모임 '서울적십자 소나무클럽' 가입...꾸준한 후원|trans-title=Soyou joins 'Seoul Red Cross Pine Tree Club', a major donor group... steady support|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/home/article/112/0003050755|via=[[Naver]]|work=Herald Muse|language=ko|last=Go|first=Seung-ah|date=July 16, 2018|access-date=March 24, 2024|archive-date=March 24, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324033345/https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/article/112/0003050755|url-status=live}}</ref>

In January 2018, Soyou held a flea market at Cure Coffee Bar with the theme "All About Soyou," where clothes, shoes, and items from her personal collection and sponsors were sold. All proceeds were then donated to the Green Umbrella Children's Foundation.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:'언니네 라디오' 소유 "플리마켓 수익금 기부했다"|url=https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/article/213/0001025562|website=TV Report|publisher=[[Naver]]|last=Kim|first=Ga-young|date=March 24, 2018|access-date=March 24, 2024|archive-date=March 24, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324034554/https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/article/213/0001025562|url-status=live}}</ref> In April 2019, she donated {{KRW|10|link=yes}} million won through the Hope Bridge National Disaster Relief Association, requesting that it be used to aid residents affected by large-scale forest fires in [[Gangwon Province, South Korea|Gangwon-do]].<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:[단독] 소유, 강원 산불 피해 복구 1000만원 기부|url=https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/article/382/0000722873|website=[[Sports Donga]]|publisher=[[Naver]]|last=Baek|first=Sol-mi|date=April 9, 2019|access-date=March 24, 2024|archive-date=March 24, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324035243/https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/article/382/0000722873|url-status=live}}</ref> In February 2020, Soyou donated {{KRW|20|link=yes}} million won through [[Good Neighbors (organization)|Good Neighbors]], an international relief and development NGO, to help prevent [[COVID-19]] among [[Daegu]] residents.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:소유, 코로나19 예방 위해 2천만원 기부 "조금이나마 도움 되길.."|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/home/article/112/0003272907|work=Herald Muse|via=[[Naver]]|last=|first=|date=February 28, 2020|access-date=March 24, 2024|archive-date=March 24, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324040053/https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/article/112/0003272907|url-status=live}}</ref>

In September 2022, [[Big Planet Made]] announced that Soyou donated {{KRW|20|link=yes}} million won to the Hope Bridge National Disaster Relief Association by adding donations to the entire sales proceeds from the flea market she held under her name in [[Gangnam District|Gangnam-gu]], [[Seoul]].<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:소유, 플리마켓 수익금 포함 2000만원 기부 "뿌듯"|url=https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/article/437/0000315375|website=JTBC News|publisher=[[Naver]]|last=Jo|first=Yeon-kyung|date=September 27, 2022|access-date=March 24, 2024|archive-date=March 24, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240324040827/https://n.news.naver.com/entertain/article/437/0000315375|url-status=live}}</ref> Later in November, she donated a total of {{KRW|20|link=yes}} million in scholarships to twenty underprivileged university students in Seoul through the Korean Red Cross Society for which Soyou acts as a public relations ambassador.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ko:소유, 대학생 20명에 장학금 2천만원 전달..선한 영향력|trans-title=Soyou delivered 20 million won in scholarships to 20 college students.. a good influence|url=https://m.entertain.naver.com/home/article/112/0003600348|via=[[Naver]]|work=Herald Muse|language=ko|last=Kim|first=Ji-hye|date=November 21, 2022|access-date=November 21, 2022|archive-date=November 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221121144157/https://entertain.naver.com/read?oid=112&aid=0003600348|url-status=live}}</ref>

