'''Clémence Beretta''' (born 27 December 1997) is a French [[race walking|race walker]]. She is a multiple-time French [[List of French records in athletics| national record]] holder.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://worldathletics.org/athletes/france/clémence-beretta-14714656 |title=Clémence BERETTA |website=World Athletics |accessdate=15 August 2026}}</ref>

==Biography==
From [[Remiremont]], she was educated at Lycée Polyvalent André Malraux in the city and is a member of the Athlé Vosges Pays de Remiremont. Beretta had a sixth place finish at the [[2022 European Athletics Championships – Women's 20 kilometres walk| 2022 European Athletics Championships]] in Munich in the  women's 20 kilometres walk in August 2022, breaking the French record for the distance which has stood for 22 years.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.tourisme-remiremont-plombieres.com/en/inspirations/clemence-beretta-a-travers-les-pas-de-la-marcheuse-vosgienne-internationale/ |title=Clémence Beretta, in the footsteps of the international Vosges walker |accessdate=15 August 2026 |website=tourisme-remiremont-plombieres.com |date=15 September 2022}}</ref>

Beretta had a sixth place finish individually, and was the first finishing Frenchwoman, with France winning the bronze medal in the team event at the [[2023 European Race Walking Team Championships]] in the Czech Republic.
<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.vosgesmatin.fr/sport/2023/05/22/clemence-beretta-et-les-bleues-ecrivent-leur-histoire#google_vignette |title=Clémence Beretta and the French women's national team are writing their history |website=vosgesmatin.fr |accessdate=15 August 2026}}</ref> Competing at  the [[2023 World Athletics Championships]] in Budapest, Hungary, she finished 16th in the 20km race. Beretta set a French record for the 10,000m race walk in January 2024 in Australia.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.centpourcent-vosges.fr/sport-vosges/nouveau-record-de-france-pour-la-marcheuse-vosgienne-clemence-beretta-sur-10-000m/ |website=centpourcent-vosges.fr |title=New French record for the Vosges walker Clémence Beretta over 10,000m! |date=27 January 2024 |first=Adel |last=Saoud |accessdate=15 August 2026}}</ref>

Beretta won the silver medal at the [[2025 European Race Walking Team Championships]] in the individual women's 20 km walk, and the gold medal in the team event alongside [[Pauline Stey]] and [[Ana Delahaie]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.athle.fr/actualites/championnats-d-europe-de-marche-par-equipes-les-bleus-ecrivent-l-histoire/21411 |title=European Team Race Walking Championships: The French make history |date=18 May 2025 |accessdate=15 August 2026 |website=Athle.fr}}</ref> In doing so, she broke her own French record for the distance she had previously set in 2024.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://remiremontvallees.com/2025/05/18/20-km-marche-championne-deurope-par-equipes-clemence-beretta-etablit-un-nouveau-record-de-france/ |website=remiremontvallees.com |accessdate=15 August 2026 |title=20km walk – European team champion Clémence Beretta sets a new French record |date=18 May 2025}}</ref>

On 15 August 2026, she placed seventh in the half marathon at the [[2026 European Athletics Championships]] in Birmingham, England.<ref>{{cite web |title=Pauline Stey just misses the podium, a Spanish one-two finish in the half-marathon walk |url=https://dicodusport.fr/blog/pauline-stey-au-pied-du-podium-double-espagnol-sur-le-semi-marathon-marche/ |date=15 August 2026 |accessdate=15 August 2026 |website=Dicodusport}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://melles750.fr/articles/2026/2026-06-03-championnats-europe-athletisme-birmingham-2026-selections-france-gressier-schrub-quinion |website=melles750.fr |accessdate=15 August 2026 |title=European Athletics Championships Birmingham 10-16 August 2026: Schrub, Gressier, Quinion, Zarbo, Beretta and 11 others selected by the FFA after the marathon runners |date=2 June 2026}}</ref>

